This is a port of Elm 2.4 PL21 for OS-9/68000Note that the following files/directories must exist for Elm towork properly:	/dd/SYS/UUCP/Domain	Contains the domain name of the system.				(ie. .chi.il.us)	/dd/SYS/UUCP/SystemID	The systems name.				(ie. SandV)	/dd/SPOOL/MAIL		Directory where mail files are stored.	/dd/USER		Directory where User HOME dirs are.	/r0			Temp files are placed hereAlso note that you will need a version of Rmail that supports multipleusernames on the command line. (Modified version of Rick Adams RMail isincluded in this archive for completeness)To install, copy all files in the "bin" directory created from this archiveto your CMDS dir, or a dir in your PATH env. var. Then, create the files:	nfrm	ufrm	ofrm	rfrm... by either copying the "frm" program to the filenames listed above,or by createing a hard link of "frm" to the files listed above.Also, you will want to create the files /dd/SYS/UUCP/Domain and/dd/SYS/UUCP/SystemID to reflect your system.That should be it, if there are any problems, please let me know so I canfix them and distribute an update...-- Paul Jerkatis - SandV BBS (708)352-0948: Chicago Area OS-9 Users Group UUCP ...{balr|tellab5}!vpnet!sandv!sysop Internet: MITHELEN@Delphi.com "RELAX! Don't worry. Have a home brew." - C. Papazian